  "description": "A security vulnerability has been detected in TeamSpeak 3 Server up to 3.13.8. This vulnerability affects unknown code of the component ECC Key Parser. Such manipulation leads to heap-based buffer overflow. The attack may be launched remotely. Upgrading to version 3.13.9 is able to resolve this issue. It is suggested to upgrade the affected component. The vendor explains: \"We have just released TeamSpeak 3 Server 3.13.9 to address a remaining variant of CVE-2026-4391, affecting ECC key parsing during the connection handshake. The original fix released with 3.13.8 did not cover this additional variant, which could allow an unauthenticated remote attacker to crash the server using specially crafted input.\"",
